ties ... collapses a mixed chain's `prompt_cache_style` to `none` whenever the chain's candidates disagree — which is why cache reads dropped to zero on 2026-08-12\"","src/rebar/llm/runner_support.py:74: `prompt_cache_style=per_candidate[0].prompt_cache_style` — follows the primary, no collapse","src/rebar/llm/runner_support.py:61-71: docstring — \"`prompt_cache_style` is the ONE exception, and follows the PRIMARY (bug 96f3): it does NOT hard-fail cross-provider ... This reverses the earlier conservative collapse — see ADR 0059 §7\""],"finding":"The Context/Problem premise that `_intersect_capabilities` 'collapses a mixed chain's prompt_cache_style to none whenever the chain's candidates disagree' is refuted by the current code: runner_support.py:74 sets `prompt_cache_style=per_candidate[0].prompt_cache_style` (follows the PRIMARY, does NOT collapse to none), and the docstring (lines 61-71) states this 'reverses the earlier conservative collapse' (bug 96f3 / ADR 0059). The collapse-to-none behavior the plan describes as current no longer exists.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f02673f3dbeb7b317","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context / Problem — sentence beginning \"_intersect_capabilities (src/rebar/llm/runner_support.py) collapses a mixed chain's prompt_cache_style to none whenever the chain's candidates disagree\"","norm_id":"na786f56b43e439af","priority":0.6611,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reader relies on the stated motivation to justify building a fallback-free ephemeral config, believing a mixed chain would still zero out cache reads today — but the primary-following fix already restores caching on the hot path even with a mixed chain."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Reword to: \"_intersect_capabilities PREVIOUSLY collapsed a mixed chain's prompt_cache_style to none on any disagreement (the cause of the 2026-08-12 zero cache reads); it now follows the primary (runner_support.py:74, ADR 0059 §7), but a mixed chain still leaves caching provider-scoped/uncertain on any call a fallback serves — motivating a genuinely homogeneous, fallback-free pinned chain.\"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add acceptance criteria + named unit tests for check_model_parity (mismatch-refusal and allow_model_change=True paths) and stamp_pass_model (correct models:{pass:model_id} shape), or explicitly remove them from this ticket's scope if deferred.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Approach: 'check_model_parity(pass_name, resolved_id, baseline_ran_model) refuses on mismatch unless allow_model_change=True.'","Approach: 'stamp_pass_model(result, pass_name, model_id) and refuse_diff_on_model_mismatch(...)'","Testing enumerates resolve_pinned_model, refuse_diff_on_model_mismatch, check_cache_effective, corpus ran_model — but NOT check_model_parity or stamp_pass_model","Acceptance Criteria list has no line for check_model_parity or stamp_pass_model"],"finding":"check_model_parity and stamp_pass_model are described as deliverable functions in the Approach ('check_model_parity(pass_name, resolved_id, baseline_ran_model) refuses on mismatch unless allow_model_change=True'; 'stamp_pass_model(result, pass_name, model_id)') but neither appears in the Testing section nor in any acceptance criterion — they are uncovered work.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdde59ffd92d59408","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach (Result stamping helper / Pinned targets bullets) vs Testing / Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n4ce86415246e0bcc","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["check_model_parity's allow_model_change branch or mismatch-refusal logic ships untested and a regression goes undetected","stamp_pass_model writes the wrong key shape and refuse_diff_on_model_mismatch can never fire because stamping never populated models:{pass:model_id}"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add ACs: 'check_model_parity refuses on resolved!=baseline mismatch, passes when equal, and honors allow_model_change=True' and 'stamp_pass_model writes model_id under models[pass_name]' with corresponding tests in test_plan_replay_parity.py.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_